          "text": "{\"stories\":[{\"id\":\"s000029\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"A well-linked search shifts agency to Nia, whose memory finds the book; the comic sacrifice and returned trolley give the ending real cost and closure.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000057\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"The failed search is honest and coherent, and choosing another book gives a gentle concrete resolution, though the middle includes several similarly paced dead ends.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000047\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Nia's knowledge of spine pictures meaningfully guides the search, and the children acknowledge the loss rather than fake success; the ending is quiet but complete.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000073\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Careful failed clues and Nia's shelf knowledge support a believable unsuccessful outcome, ending clearly with a different book and lingering disappointment.\",\"group_id\":1},{\"id\":\"s000034\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Sorting the returns directly reveals the missing book, and Nia's bookmark plus Lio's lost comic make the recovered-book ending concrete and consequential.\",\"group_id\":2},{\"id\":\"s000043\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Nia claims a role in directing the search, then remembers the window seat and finds the book; the final shared page and lost comic provide satisfying closure.\",\"group_id\":0},{\"id\":\"s000068\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"A current catalogue clue and Nia's picture-label skill lead to the book behind the fox title; the ending responsibly returns borrowed items and preserves the sacrifice.\",\"group_id\":3},{\"id\":\"s000096\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Despite an unhelpful desk and a false window-seat memory, the updated catalogue and picture labels lead to recovery; the emotional ending is concrete and earned.\",\"group_id\":3},{\"id\":\"s000005\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":8,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Nia's increased agency and the current catalogue support a clear shelf discovery, while the bookmark, trolley, and missed comic make the resolution tangible.\",\"group_id\":3},{\"id\":\"s000085\",\"rating\":{\"coherence\":8,\"style\":7,\"grammar\":9,\"storytelling\":7,\"overall\":8},\"note\":\"Safe refusal to use an unstable ladder and several checked leads support the unsuccessful search; Nia's bookmark returned to her pocket gives the bittersweet ending a concrete image.\",\"group_id\":1}],\"diversity\":{\"premise\":1,\"causal_path\":4,\"ending\":4,\"language\":3,\"overall\":3},\"diversity_evidence\":\"All ten stories share the same missing-book-before-closing premise, cast, setting, promise, and recurring prose blocks. There are meaningful but limited branches: recovery from the window seat (s000029, s000043), returns trolley (s000034), or picture-labeled shelf after a current catalogue clue (s000005, s000068, s000096), versus an honest unsuccessful search and substitute book (s000047, s000057, s000073, s000085). These variations do not establish diversity across the full generator.\",\"plot_groups\":[{\"group_id\":0,\"summary\":\"Nia gains agency and remembers the window-seat hiding place, where the missing book is recovered.\"},{\"group_id\":1,\"summary\":\"The children pursue and exhaust plausible clues without finding the book, then leave with a substitute while acknowledging disappointment.\"},{\"group_id\":2,\"summary\":\"Careful sorting of returned books reveals the missing book on the trolley.\"},{\"group_id\":3,\"summary\":\"A current catalogue location and Nia's picture-label knowledge guide the children to the book on the animal shelf.\"}]}"
        }
